The config error confirms the lever's shape: `disable` takes an array of rule ids, not a boolean. So the exact fix is `"disable": ["unchecked-throwing-call-python"]`, applied in a fresh session since pi-lens reads config at startup.

tool: bash({"command": "cd <PATH> && cat > .pi-lens.json <<'EOF'
{
  "$schema": "<URL>",
  "rules": {
    "unchecked-throwing-call-python": { "disable": ["unchecked-throwing-call-python"] }
  }
}
EOF
python3 -c "import json;json.load(open('.pi-lens.json'));print('valid')""})
